I've been playing nethack for a few years off and on, and never
really gotten a character past level 8, so my recent death in the
astral plane was an extremely big leap forward for me. Be warned, this
post is pretty long, and contains spoilers.

I started as a neutral Valkyrie (on nethack.alt.org) and quickly found
boots of speed, which made me very powerful in the beginning. I was
clearing out the gnomish mines when I started to get a little nervous
about my hp, and started engrave-testing wands. Imagine my surprise
when the following comes up: "You may wish for any item."
Determined not to screw this up, I looked up a wishing spoiler and
studied it carefully. My first wish netted me one blessed scroll of
charging (I asked for two). My second and third (yes, three! How
fortunate!) wishes were for a SDSM and gauntlets of power, both with +2
enchants. Thinking I was a clever person, I zapped my empty wand until
I got another wish, and cooked up a cloak of magic resist. The wand
then disintegrated, and I realized what I had done. This was mistake
#1. However, I still had a set of ridiculous gear, so I plugged on with
my new -9 ish AC. I finished up the mines with reckless abandon, and
got a bag of holding somewhere.

Next I headed to Sokoban. Everything went pretty well, since nothing
could touch me, except a grey unicorn got stuck behind a boulder and I
had to kill it. Unfortunately, I couldn't kill it without my gear so
I decided to break the boulder and then kill it, since it was already
hostile. Odin was not pleased. I reached the end and got another bag of
holding.

I plugged away until level 10, where I finally found an altar. Thankful
that I left the black unicorn alive, I was dismayed to see that it was
chaotic. I started to descend deeper, my bags brimming with
unidentified crap (even wands - very dangerous). As I backtracked to
level 10, I found a white unicorn and promptly murdered it. It's
sacrifice converted the altar, and the black unicorn's mollified
Odin. I engraved Elbereth next to the altar, and started playing with
some wands. I zapped a wand and it changed the engraving to some
fortune, so clearly this is a wand of enlightenment. I zap myself and
bam - I'm a silver dragon. It's kind of cool, but I was weaker, and
my cloak broke. After it wore off I pressed on, and few create monsters
later and I was in good with the big guy and holding a shiny new
Mjolnir; I headed down.

A few floors below, I hear a telepathic plea. Ignoring it, I stumble
into a magic portal where my quest leader tells me I'll die, and to
go get more experience. I give her the finger and she boots me back to
the dungeon, and I decide to continue downwards.

At what I later learned was Medusa's isle, I used a wand of cold and
earth to make my way to the structure, and burst in unannounced.
Medusa's gaze hit me, reflected, and stoned her before I even knew
what happened. I tore up the statues and headed down.

At this point, I was still struggling with unidentified scrolls,
potions, rings, and wands. I managed to identify some through use
(including a ring of levitation that would be useful later) and
realized I was doing very well on this attempt, but my utter lack of
knowledge about anything except the upper levels almost got me killed
once. At this point I started hitting the spoilers pretty hard,
determined to make this run count. I moved through a couple levels of
maze, and after realizing I could destroy walls, I made neat paths
between the stairs.

I arrived at the castle and saw the drawbridge down. Worried about all
I read about drawbridges being deathtraps, I used my ring of levitation
to go to the back, and over the trap doors. It took a while of standing
in one spot hitting things, but the entire throne room was eventually
killed on one neat pile, and I went in and sat on the throne.
Unfortunately, this cursed one of my bags of holding, and I had to
evacuate it's contents to the other bag and dump it. I slaughtered
the dragons and retrieved the castle's wand of wishing, and cooked up
some new +2 speed boots, another +2 MR cloak, and a magic marker. I
used the marker to write some blessed identify scrolls, which helped
alleviate my problem slightly.

With all the experience from the castle, I went to do my quest, finally
being level 14. I kicked the crap out of everything, even though some
giant had a wand of create monster he emptied when I couldn't reach
him. I got the orb and bell and went back down.

It was time to take the plunge. I fell through a trapdoor, and entered
the valley of the dead. The sheer number of creatures streaming through
walls at me told me that this was going to take a while. I'm pretty
sure I killed my own ghost about three times, and offed some ghosts of
others as well. Making it to the down stair, I hit the twisting maze of
Gehennom. Gehennom is big. Really big. Maze after maze gets really
boring, and with uncontrolled teleportitis, really annoying. But, I
moved forward, making paths to the staircases on most levels that I
could, and murdering all sorts of stuff, until I came to Asmodeus'
lair. I got the honor of fighting him and Baezulbub at the same time.
After a very long fight and something blinding me, I figured I should
go after them when they teleport away. I move to the stairs, chase them
across the upstairs maze level, and flatten them both.

It's more mazes from here on in, until I get to Vlad's tower and
get the candelabrum. Still not having teleport control, I give in and
wish myself up a blessed ring of teleport control. Let me tell you,
controlled teleport is really, really cool. I invoke my orb of fate,
set the dial to level 10, and POOF! There I am. I buy some candles,
bless my bag of holding, grease some stuff, and teleport to level 47.
Well, not really. But now with -17 AC and a +4 superhammer, I'm at
the valley of the dead and ready to get the amulet. I descend a level
and orb myself for real to level 47. I trudge downwards until I find
both fake wizard towers, and finally, the square. I engrave Elbereth
with a wand of fire, dump my candelabrum and bell, and head up to kill
Rodney.

I'm working my way up Rodney's tower, and I see a master mind
flayer. Thinking I am invincible, I attack it and it mind-sucks me.
Crap. I zap it with a wand of death, it misses, sucks me again, and I
zap it again and it dies. I try to assess the damage. Not too bad. I
pull stuff out of my bag and write up a blessed identify scroll hoping
I can re-identify everything important. No luck with getting everything
identified, I go for the only scroll that was unidentified in my bag
before getting sucked, hoping it's a genocide scroll. Nope, it's a
blessed scroll of amnesia. I dump it and cram everything back into my
bag - I'll sort it out later. I still sorta remem- oh crap. In goes
the wand of canceling that got un-identified, blowing up the bag and
all my reserve gear. Crap, crap crap. Fortunately, the super-important
stuff was outside the bag (unicorn horn, levitation ring, lizard
corpse, some digging wands, 2x amulets of life saving, and a wand of
death). I decide that since my wand of wishing was gone, I was going to
press on. I headed up and confronted Rodney.

I destroy everything around Rodney's chamber, freeze the moat and dig
into his house. Rodney and his goons come out, and I start beating
them. He makes more goons, I beat them too. Uh uo, my HP is getting a
little low... I zap him with the wand of death, only to find out it's
empty. Miraculously, I finish everything off with my hammer, and take
back the stuff he stole from me. With the book in hand, I fumble
through the levels back to the vibrating square, perform the ritual and
descend.

Initially, everything is as easy as usual. I make it to the courtyard
door and stand there killing stuff that comes in. Gee, these priests
hit hard, and there sure are a lot of them. Hmm, my HP is getting low.
Oh crap, dead. Thank Odin for that amulet. I equip the other one, and
resolve to be more careful. I clear enough to get inside and walk
around, and quickly break my resolution. Goodbye to the second amulet.
Third time is a charm, right? I pick up some cockatrice corpses, and
find the door to the temple. I tallywhack the priest and two Rodneys
inside with the cockatrices and realize I have no means of getting my
orb back from the statue. After some wandering around the level for a
pick, I remember I know force bolt, and go bust up my statues. I begin
the ascent.

Picking up rations and eating stuff as I go along, I'm doing pretty
well. I have forgotten most of the maps, but the cut paths to the
stairway make navigation slightly easier. Rodney appears, less often
that I had thought he would, and never manages to steal the amulet.
That level-bumping down is annoying, but controlled teleportitis is
really cool. About halfway up through hell, I walk through a door and
am hit by a potion of paralysis. It was thrown by a master mind flayer.
This could be bad. He sucks the grease from my hat, and my brain down
to int 4 before I am un-paralyzed. I smack him with my hammer, and
continue on, thankful I wasn't killed. Shortly after, the mail daemon
arrives, and someone points out I almost died. I was being watched.

I continued up, despite Rodney's appearances and Moloch's kind
invitations to levels I just went through. After getting out of hell,
it was almost a cakewalk. On the way up, I nab a bunch of K-rations and
other food. I find my altar, sacrifice and pray, but Odin doesn't
even uncurse any of my stuff. I replace my cursed unicorn horn, and
continue on. I finally make it - level 1 - I am pretty excited. The
mail daemon arrives, with a message from the same person - "First
level!!!" I ascend to the planes.

At the plane of earth, Rodney shows up and gets three-shotted. Boom. I
try to read the spellbook of dig, and get knocked out while something
beats on me. I name it oops to try and amuse my audience, and remember
I have wands of digging. I pull 'em out and start searching. Finding
the portal wasn't too bad, and I go up to the plane of air. I equip
levitation and start beating up monsters. Those air elementals are
pretty tough, and I almost bite it in a couple of places. Thankfully I
had some full healing potions. I fly around and find the portal to the
plane of fire. Hey, this looks like my quest place! I start beating up
everything, and realize I'm not doing so hot. I barely make it out of
the entrance mobs, and wait around to recover some HP. I then float
around the level, killing stuff and looking for the portal. After
nearly clearing the map, I head up to the plane of water. Right off the
bat, an Archon wields demonbane and starts smacking me. It hurts, and
I'm surrounded. I am forced to retreat, and fortunately it couldn't
see me. I clear out the right half of the level, and then move to clear
the left. The level is clean except for 2 mobs when I finally find the
portal and arrive on the astral plane.

Well, where to go? Figuring I have to pick randomly, I ask my friend.
He suggests I go left, and I do. I've got this angel, and some
potions of healing, what could go wrong? Hey there's Death. He gets
dropped in three hits, what a chump. My angel and I start clearing the
first left room. Death gets up and I kill him again - wait, what? I
only have 93 max hit points now. Curse you Death! I start penetrating
into the temple courtyard. For some reason, an Angel of Odin begins
beating me up from behind. I am forced to kill it. Death comes along
again, and I kill him too. Mercifully, a priest of Moloch makes a wall
of insects for me to hide behind (on both sides) and recover HP. I
engrave Elbereth in the doorway with a wand of fire I found, and start
pushing inwards. After everything is dead save a couple of ants, I move
into the temple. I check the altar - chaotic. Well darn. I sigh and
head back to the entrance. I get to kill Death again, and now my max HP
is down to 63. My pet shows up, finally, and we head to the center
door. After a few things are killed, Pestilence comes out and sprays me
with goo. I stab myself with a unicorn horn and all is well. Well, not
really, I'm not doing so hot on HP. Pestilence dies, and we keep
going. Then he gets up and hits me with his disease again. The unicorn
horn doesn't cure it, and I'm really low on HP. I start to panic. I
try the horn again, nothing. Then he smacks me and I get the dreaded
message - "You die ..." I hope the person watching me wasn't
too disappointed.

Looking back, I should have prayed. Also, I think I knew restore
ability, so disrobing and casting that might have restored my HP and
given me a better chance. Perhaps I should have re-geared for the trip
to the planes (I now appreciate wands of death more).

This was my first real attempt at ascension, and I got really far. I
figure I had a 1/3 chance of ascending, and would be cheering right now
if that altar had been neutral. I will try again, in time. If you have
read the story this far, thanks for listening to the tale of Wahzor the
Valkyrie, who almost made it. I'm posting this to tell the story, to
boast a little at how far I got, asking for some advice for next time,
and perhaps a little sympathy.

